      "math_academy_id": "e-5417",
      "problem": "Which of the following matrices have a rank of $4?$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14129652/assets/afae1d6c7277f5b22e6c7a3023968a226beb9b86b0945b7a974159a61b6688a8.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that a matrix of rank $4$ must have at least $4$ columns and at least $4$ rows. \nSo, we disregard the matrix $B$ since it has only $3$ rows. \n\nAlso, the matrix must have $4$ pivot columns. As we can see, the matrix $A$ has only $3$ pivot columns, while the matrix $C$ has exactly $4$ pivot columns. So, $\\textrm{rank}(A)=3$ and $\\textrm{rank}(C)=4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$C$ only\".",
